    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0426" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1946v01/pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.AA/6–2946: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-07-03T20:00:00-04:00">July 3, 1946—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>113. Bevin told SEC Paris July 3 that Brit Govt expects to inform Ireland that
                    Brit will support its candidacy for UN membership.</p>
                <p>Since Brit are approaching Irish, and in view of De Valera’s<anchor n="99"
                        xml:id="d213-f1"/> probable negative attitude (urtels 70, June 26[<hi
                        rendition="#italic">27</hi>] and 72 June 29),<anchor n="1" xml:id="d213-f2"
                    /> we have decided not (repeat not) to make any approach to Irish at this time.
                    Please inform us of Irish reaction to British approach.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d213-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d213-f1" n="99" xml:id="d213-f1-content">
                <p>Eamon De Valera, Prime Minister of Eire.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d213-f2" n="1" xml:id="d213-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d213-f3" n="2" xml:id="d213-f3-content">
                <p>Repeated to New York as telegram 129.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
